From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:38:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: a native ARM64 child that remaps its image keeps
 running it

World of Warcraft's ARM64 client replaces its image with a section of
its own: NtCreateSection(SEC_COMMIT | SEC_NO_CHANGE, SizeOfImage), a
read-write view, a copy of the image there, NtUnmapViewOfSection of the
image, then three views of the section at the image's base (code RX,
.data RW, the rest RO). It then decrypts its code a function at a time
through the read-write view, with FlushInstructionCache on each, and
runs it at the base. In a native ARM64 child the base is the image's
JIT-pool copy (0262), 16 KB aligned, so the views failed alignment and
the client jumped into still encrypted bytes at +0xb3790.

Decision 0176, amended: a view of a plain section mapped at a presented
copy's address is mapped where the image's PE view was, its bytes are
copied into the copy through the pool's RW alias, x18-patched and
flushed, and the caller gets the copy's address. Every view a native
child maps of a plain section is recorded with the section's file and
offset (the records grow as needed; none is dropped for a new one); a
FlushInstructionCache on one whose section is also mapped at a copy
brings the flushed bytes into the copy the same way, but for the words
patched there already, and one on a presented copy x18-patches the
range. Such a flush patches the code its first word reaches, up to a
RET, BR, their pointer-authenticated forms or a UDF.

In a native child's image the x18 patcher passes over encrypted 1 KB
windows of .text (more than 8 of 256 words in the unallocated encoding
groups, which no compiler emits): a patched word there decrypted to
garbage. The trampoline reservation still counts them, so the code
decrypted there later has room. Images in x86-64 and ARM64EC processes,
and a child's copy of ntdll, are patched whole, as before. A native
child's copy gets every relocation, as Windows' loader applies them:
the client has 95 on encrypted .text words, which were skipped.

Linear: PLA-514
Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md, tools/tests/test_x18_encrypted.py
Offered-upstream: no
